# Single-page app fallback.
#
# The router uses real paths, so a customer who reloads on /store, or opens a
# product link someone sent them, asks the static host for a file that does not
# exist. Without this rule the host answers 404 and the site looks broken for
# every URL except the home page.
#
# Netlify and Render both read this file. The 200 matters: a 302 would change
# the address bar and lose the route.
/*    /index.html   200
